From: Adam Matthews <52178922+adamsthws@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 20:10:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] esp32c3 wifi: write a received frame only where the
 hardware would

The fork wrote each received frame through the next receive descriptor
whether or not the driver had handed it over, and however big the buffer.
Writing into buffers the driver had taken back corrupted its heap, which then
failed in free() (tlsf_free) - seen as a crash when the plug's Wi-Fi stopped.
A frame is now written only into a descriptor the driver owns with room for
it, and dropped otherwise, as the hardware drops it. Offered upstream as
lcgamboa/qemu #13.
---
 hw/misc/esp32c3_wifi.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/misc/esp32c3_wifi.c b/hw/misc/esp32c3_wifi.c
index df9d964..6b14720 100644
--- a/hw/misc/esp32c3_wifi.c
+++ b/hw/misc/esp32c3_wifi.c
@@ -179,6 +179,21 @@ void Esp32_sendFrame(Esp32WifiState *s, mac80211_frame *frame,int length, int si
     // do a DMA transfer from the hardware to esp32 memory
     dma_list_item item;
     address_space_read(&address_space_memory, s->dma_inlink_ptr, MEMTXATTRS_UNSPECIFIED, &item, 12);
+    /* Autoflash emulator: write only where real hardware would - a descriptor the
+     * driver has handed over (owner set), with room for the frame. Writing
+     * anywhere else corrupts the guest's heap, which then fails in free(). A
+     * frame with nowhere to go is dropped, as the hardware drops it. */
+    if (!item.owner || item.address == 0 || item.size < length) {
+        static int shown;
+        if (shown < 20) {
+            shown++;
+            printf("WIFIDMA: frame dropped - descriptor %08x owner=%u size=%u, frame %d bytes\n",
+                   s->dma_inlink_ptr, item.owner, item.size, length);
+            fflush(stdout);
+        }
+        free(header);
+        return;
+    }
     address_space_write(&address_space_memory, item.address, MEMTXATTRS_UNSPECIFIED, header, length);
     item.length=length;
     item.eof=1;
